      "native_axes": [
        {
          "name": "n_and_total_n",
          "upper_inclusive": 300000,
          "proposed_l2_upper_inclusive": 600000
        }
      ],
      "native_invariants": "q1..10000;1<=k<=n;positionsdistinct1..n;ti1..10^9;sourceinput permits blankseparatorline",
      "source_evidence": [
        {
          "line": 1,
          "text": "On a strip of land of length n there are k air conditioners: the i-th air conditioner is placed in cell a_i (1 ≤ a_i ≤ n). Two or more air conditioners cannot be placed in the same cell (i.e. all a_i are distinct)."
        },
        {
          "line": 5,
          "text": "![Original illustration 1](https://espresso.codeforces.com/d603b553d049b7bf9a634f173e94f1e4d86e0053.png) Example of strip of length n=6, where k=2, a=[2,5] and t=[14,16]."
        },
        {
          "line": 7,
          "text": "For each cell i (1 ≤ i ≤ n) find it's temperature, that can be calculated by the formula $$$min_{1 ≤ j ≤ k}(t_j + |a_j - i|),$$$"
        },
        {
          "line": 28,
          "text": "The first line contains one integer q (1 ≤ q ≤ 10^4) — the number of test cases in the input. Then test cases follow. Before each test case, there is an empty line."
        },
        {
          "line": 30,
          "text": "Each test case contains three lines. The first line contains two integers n (1 ≤ n ≤ 3 ⋅ 10^5) and k (1 ≤ k ≤ n) — the length of the strip of land and the number of air conditioners respectively."
        },
        {
          "line": 32,
          "text": "The second line contains k integers a_1, a_2, …, a_k (1 ≤ a_i ≤ n) — positions of air conditioners on the strip of land."
        },
        {
          "line": 34,
          "text": "The third line contains k integers t_1, t_2, …, t_k (1 ≤ t_i ≤ 10^9) — temperatures of air conditioners."
        },
        {
          "line": 36,
          "text": "It is guaranteed that the sum of n over all test cases does not exceed 3 ⋅ 10^5."
        }
      ],
      "status": "contract_transcription_for_implementation;L2proposal_not_yet_validated",
      "preserve_other_native_bounds": true
    }
  },
